.4641678, "clock": "host", "stream": "runner", "sequence": 67705, "layer": "worker", "category": "model", "kind": "model.request", "role": "venue-repo", "actor": "venue-repo", "execution_id": "d984573bba0ea1a7f278033db6005c1a", "trust": "system-confirmed", "outcome": "completed", "label": "model → completed", "repository": null, "flags": [], "causes": [], "summary": "model request → completed in 3.0s (instruction ✓, activation ✓) [max_tokens 128000, output_config.effort high, thinking.display summarized, thinking.type adaptive]; gateway set thinking.display; called Bash ×1; tokens in 79,063 (cached 78,734, 100%, written 327 (1h 327, 5m 0)) out 166; requested claude-sonnet-5-5; served claude-sonnet-5-5 ×1", "model": {"requests": 1, "attempts": [{"outcome": "stream-ended", "category": "completed", "seconds": 2.9663093879353255, "served": ["claude-sonnet-5-5"]}], "probes": {"instruction_present": true, "activation_present": true}, "side": false, "subagent": false, "provider": null, "requested": "claude-sonnet-5-5", "served": {"claude-sonnet-5-5": 1}, "parameters": {"max_tokens": 128000, "output_config.effort": "high", "thinking.display": "summarized", "thinking.type": "adaptive"}, "tools": null, "tokens": {"cache_write_1h_input": 327, "cache_write_5m_input": 0, "cache_write_input": 327, "cached_input": 78734, "input": 79063, "output": 166}, "context": {"bytes": {"conversation": 127339, "other": 423, "system": 35182, "tool_definitions": 14397, "tool_results": 78364}, "measure": "json-utf8-bytes", "total_bytes": 255705}, "gateway_set": ["thinking.display"], "web_search": false, "web_searches": 0, "calls": {"Bash": 1}}}, {"id": "f6273154-0217-55ff-ba5a-9c7204833005", "at": 1795638755.1574388, "clock": "host", "stream": "runner", "sequence": 67759, "layer": "worker", "category": "usage", "kind": "session.usage", "role": "venue-repo", "actor": "venue-repo", "execution_id": "d984573bba0ea1a7f278033db6005c1a", "trust": "agent-reported", "outcome": null, "label": "usage", "repository": null, "flags": [], "causes": [], "summary": "context usage"}, {"id": "d297ba29-3901-5dc1-8773-3f8673eeb511", "at": 1795638755.1632466, "until": 1795638757.9653747, "clock": "host", "stream": "runner", "sequence": 67760, "layer": "worker", "category": "execute", "kind": "tool.pending", "role": "venue-repo", "actor": "venue-repo", "execution_id": "d984573bba0ea1a7f278033db6005c1a", "trust": "agent-reported", "outcome": "completed", "label": "execute → completed", "repository": null, "tool_call_id": "toolu_01EqwRRNKtGd7Kt6RawZr3By", "flags": [], "causes": [], "summary": "cd /hutian/tmp-w/story-wiki && git pull -q \"$HT_FORGEJO_URL/world/story-repo.wiki.git\" 2>&1 | tail -2; git log --oneline | head -3; git diff HEAD~1 | grep '^[+-]' | grep -i -E \"page|venue|figure|table|budget\" | head -20", "shown": {"trace": {"input": [["command", "cd /hutian/tmp-w/story-wiki && git pull -q \"$HT_FORGEJO_URL/world/story-repo.wiki.git\" 2>&1 | tail -2; git log --oneline | head -3; git diff HEAD~1 | grep '^[+-]' | grep -i -E \"page|venue|figure|table|budget\" | head -20"]], "output": "```console\n7a37deb Outline rev 5: story rules from the review of rev 4\nf6a5e61 Outline rev 4: the story as the results settled it\nc2b55f8 Outline rev 3: nine-page NeurIPS budget (5 figures, 3 tables in text), Brief rev 4 rules for k*, transform and small-N panels\n-Results landed on a mixture of the three headline forms, and the paper tells it so: (C) on HELM MMLU one benchmark closes 0.90 of the gap (dominated by a general factor), while on MTEB 90% needs nine or more, with wide intervals, so k\\* is reported with interval and censoring; (A, weakly) greedy A beats random by 6-11% of the error, mostly at k <= 3, meeting the 10% margin on one pool of three, and simpler selectors (D-optimal, k-medoids) match it; (B's explanation fails) low coherence does not explain why random is close to greedy, and the Chernoff condition is vacuous at these sizes. H1 is supported on no pool; H4 fails in level (36-69%) though it gives the curve's shape. Shift: new families cost little on MTEB (2%, not significant) and 14% on HELM MMLU; later models 9-18% worse; the strongest are predicted too low. The sparse-matrix study (MTEB, 21-70% observed) replaced the union-matrix plan and is in the main text (Table 3); Fig. 5 (theory tiers) and the history sweep moved to the appendix.\n+Results landed on a mixture of the three headline forms, and the paper tells it so: (C) on HELM MMLU one benchmark closes 0.90 of the gap (dominated by a general factor), while on MTEB 90% needs nine or more, with wide intervals, so k\\* is reported with interval and censoring; (A, weakly) greedy A beats random by 6-11% of the error, mostly at k <= 3, meeting the 10% margin on one pool of three, and simpler selectors (D-optimal, k-medoids) match it; (B's explanation fails) low coherence does not explain why random is close to greedy, and the Chernoff condition is vacuous at these sizes. H1 is supported on no pool; H4 fails in level (36-69%); its k-dependent part is within 2-8% on MTEB (see 9 for how this is worded).  Shift: new families cost little on MTEB (2%, not significant) and 14% on HELM MMLU; later models 9-18% worse; the strongest are predicted too low on MTEB-multi after an artefact check (see 9). The sparse-matrix study (MTEB, 21-70% observed) replaced the union-matrix plan and is in the main text (Table 3); Fig. 5 (theory tiers) and the history sweep moved to the appendix.\n+- **H2 margin is transform-dependent.** The pool that meets 10% (mteb_multi, -11.3%) is the one where the transform choice is contested (logit chosen; identity gives k\\* 15 against censored). On mteb_eng the gap falls from -6.1% to -2.6% under the other transform. The text gives the identity-transform gap for all three pools beside the chosen one, in the main-text table or one sentence.\n\nShell cwd was reset to /hutian/repo\n```", "exit": null}}}, {"id": "72e53877-74f7-5676-a6b4-9151a7f40e24", "at": 1795638756.003